<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Power profile for the Ulefone Armor 29 Pro (GQ5012BF1, MT6878).

  Replaces the vendor placeholder (generic MediaTek values: 3/4 CPU speeds per
  cluster that this SoC does not have, all modem values 0, capacity 21200),
  which left CPU out of Battery usage entirely.

  Units: mA in the fuel gauge's (sh366003) units, the same units Android uses
  for capacity and drain on this phone.

  MEASURED 2026-11-15 on the phone, on battery, screen off, wakelock held,
  frequencies pinned, 24 gauge samples per point (median):
    cpu.core_power.*  per-core increment of 1 vs 2 busy cores at each frequency,
                      fitted as a*f + b*f^3 (little: 2.28/1.26, big: 20.10/4.06)
    cpu.cluster_power / cpu.active   1-core minus 2-core increment (~1 mA)
    cpu.idle          awake idle 82.5 mA minus the suspend floor
    cpu.suspend       screen-off overnight drain, 5 % of 8874 mAh in 9.9 h
                      at 1 % awake (batterystats history 2026-11-15 04:31-14:27)
  NOT MEASURED (vendor values kept): screen, ambient, wifi, bluetooth, gps,
  audio, video, camera, radio.*.  The modem needs a <modem> block before
  mobile radio can be attributed; not added without a measurement.
-->
<device name="Android">
    <item name="battery.capacity">10600</item>

    <array name="cpu.clusters.cores">
